is &#x02013; A diagnostic pitfall for the internist</article-title><source>Archives of Internal Medicine</source><year>1963</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>491</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14051367</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b6-mjm11_2p164"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heusner</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nontuberculous spinal epidural infections</article-title><source>New England Journal of Medicine</source><year>1948</year><volume>239</volume><fpage>845</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18894306</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7-mjm11_2p164"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meyers</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiner</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Diagnosis of hematogenous pyogenic vertebral osteomyelitis by magnetic resonance imaging</article-title><source>Archives of Internal Medicine</source><year>1991</year><volume>151</volume><fpage>683</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2012449</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-mjm11_2p164"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Modic</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Feiglin</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Piraino</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Vertebral osteomyelitis: Assessment using MR</article-title><source>Radiology</source><year>1985</year><volume>157</volume><fpage>157</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3875878</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-mjm11_2p164"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bamberger</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Di